# Nim / nimble
nimcache/
nimblecache/
*.exe
build/
public/
.nimble/
.direnv/

# `nim c -r` writes an extensionless native binary next to the source unless
# `-o:` is given, and `just test` does not give one for every suite.
tests/test_dev
src/ssr
src/build
write_nim_cfg

# The sibling `--path`s, as absolute paths. Both `just nim-cfg` and
# `repro.nim`'s `docs-book-nim-cfg` action generate this file, and its contents
# are machine-specific. Ignoring it is what keeps somebody's `/home/<name>/...`
# out of a commit; it must stay untracked, because a committed copy would
# collide with the one the build generates.
nim.cfg

# `nim js` writes its output next to the compiled .nim file unless -o: is given.
src/**/*.js
tests/**/*.js
